WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.802
Use this slide as a roadmap.

00:00:01.802 --> 00:00:07.152
The ideas are intentionally ordered so later examples build on earlier concepts.

00:00:07.152 --> 00:00:12.917
As you move forward, keep asking how the new idea connects to the larger analytics workflow instead of

00:00:12.917 --> 00:00:16.242
treating each method as an isolated command.

00:00:16.242 --> 00:00:20.027
Machine learning is a workflow rather than a single fit command.

00:00:20.027 --> 00:00:25.517
Keep training information separate from evaluation data, compare against a baseline,

00:00:25.517 --> 00:00:29.982
and interpret model performance in the context of the real prediction problem.

00:00:29.982 --> 00:00:35.742
Before moving on, explain the main idea in one sentence without reading the slide.

00:00:35.742 --> 00:00:41.160
That quick explanation is a useful check that the concept is becoming reusable knowledge.
